<description>One new USEM Qualys CI lookup rule, 415 Device Name Match, for the device classes the CMDB keeps outside the Hardware tree: IP Phone extends the base CI class directly and Scanner sits under Imaging Hardware, so the hardware-wide name rules never see those records and the class rules need an OS that a phone or a scanner does not report. The rule looks for the scanned host name in exactly those two classes (one device carrying the name is the match, the scanned address breaks a tie), and refuses a host whose OS names a server or desktop system. It resolves the contact-centre phones (cc.bofa.com, named avx plus the MAC tail) and the check scanners that stay unmatched today. No existing rule changes; no system property is read or shipped.</description>
